uld</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Shors</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Is there a link between adult neurogenesis and learning?</article-title><source>Hippocampus</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>216</fpage><lpage>224</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16421862</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Amrein1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Amrein</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Slomianka</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Lipp</surname><given-names>HP</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Granule cell number, cell death and cell proliferation in the dentate gyrus of wild-living rodents.</article-title><source>Eur J Neurosci</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>3342</fpage><lpage>3350</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15610166</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Amrein2"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Amrein</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Slomianka</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Poletaeva</surname><suffix>II</suffix></name><name><surname>Bologova</surname><given-names>NV</given-names></name><name><surname>Lipp</surname><given-names>HP</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Marked species and age-dependent differences in cell proliferation and neurogenesis in the hippocampus of wild-living rodents.</article-title><source>Hippocampus</source><volume>14</volume><fpage>1000</fpage><lpage>1010</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15390172</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Starborg1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Starborg</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gell</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Brundell</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>H&#x000f6;&#x000f6;g</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>The murine Ki-67 cell proliferation antigen accumulates in the nucleolar and heterochromatic regions of interphase cells and at the periphery of the mitotic chromosomes in a process essential for cell cycle progression.</article-title><source>J Cell Sci</source><volume>109</volume><fpage>143</fpage><lpage>153</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8834799</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Tye1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tye</surname><given-names>BK</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>MCM proteins in DNA replication.</article-title><source>Annu Rev Biochem</source><volume>68</volume><fpage>649</fpage><lpage>686</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10872463</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Matsuo1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Matsuo</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Kawamoto</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Matsubara</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Okubo</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Cloning and developmental expression of the murine homolog of doublecortin.</article-title><source>Biochem Biophys Res Commun</source><volume>252</volume><fpage>571</fpage><lpage>576</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9837748</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Lee1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Basic helix-loop-helix genes in neural development.</article-title><source>Curr Opin Neurobiol</source><volume>7</volume><fpage>13</fpage><lpage>20</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9039799</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Scholzen1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scholzen</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Gerdes</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>The Ki-67 protein: from the known and the unknown.</article-title><source>J Cell Physiol</source><volume>182</volume><fpage>311</fpage><lpage>322</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10653597</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Cameron1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cameron</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name><name><surname>McKay</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Adult neurogenesis produces a large pool of new granule cells in the dentate gyrus.</article-title><source>J Comp Neurol</source><volume>435</volume><fpage>406</fpage><lpage>417</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11406822</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Hayes1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hayes</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name><name><surname>Nowakowski</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Dynamics of cell proliferation in the adult dentate gyrus of two inbred strains of mice.</article-title><source>Brain Res Dev Brain Res</source><volume>134</volume><fpage>77</fpage><lpage>85</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Decher1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Decher</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Fahr</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title><italic>Hipposideros cyclops</italic>.</article-title><source>Mamm species</source><volume>763</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>7</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Thiele1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thiele</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Winter</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Hierarchical strategy for relocating food targets in flower bats: spatial memory versus cue-directed search.</article-title><source>Anim Behav</source><volume>69</volume><fpage>315</fpage><lpage>327</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Winter1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Winter</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Stich</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Foraging in a complex naturalistic environment: capacity of spatial working memory in flower bats.</article-title><source>J Exp Biol</source><volume>208</volume><fpage>539</fpage><lpage>548</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15671342</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-AlvarezBuylla1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Alvarez-Buylla</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirn</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Birth, migration, incorporation, and death of vocal control neurons in adult songbirds.</article-title><source>J Neurobiol</source><volume>33</volume><fpage>585</fpage><lpage>601</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9369461</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Lavenex1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lavenex</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Steele</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobs</surname><given-names>LF</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>The seasonal pattern of cell proliferation and neuron number in the dentate gyrus of wild adult eastern grey squirrels.</article-title><source>Eur J Neurosci</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>643</fpage><lpage>648</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10712644</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Kuhn1"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kuhn</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name><name><surname>Dickinson-Anson</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Gage</surname><given-names>FH</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Neurogenesis in the dentate gyrus of the adult rat: age-related decrease of neuronal progenitor proliferation.</article-title><source>J Neurosci</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>2027</fpage><lpage>2033</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8604047</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Fahrner1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fahrner</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kann</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Flubacher</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Heinrich</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Freiman</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Granule cell dispersion is not accompanied by enhanced neurogenesis in temporal lobe epilepsy patients.</article-title><source>Exp Neurol</source><volume>203</volume><fpage>320</fpage><lpage>332</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17049346</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Wilkinson1"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilkinson</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>South</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Life history, ecology and longevity in bats.</article-title><source>Aging Cell</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>124</fpage><lpage>131</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12882342</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Belsky1"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Belsky</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name></person-group><year>1990</year><source>The psychology of aging: theory, research and interventions</source><publisher-loc>Monterey, CA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Brooks/Cole</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Horn1"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Horn</surname><given-names>JIE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1970</year><article-title>Organization of data on life-span development of human abilities.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Goulet</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Baltes</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name></person-group><source>Life-span developmental psychology: Research and theory</source><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Academic Press</publisher-name><fpage>423</fpage><lpage>466</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000455-Stich1"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stich</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name><name><surname>Winter</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Lack of generalization of object discrimination between spatial contexts by a bat.</article-title><source>J Exp Biol</sour